  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 1.6.3, package-lock.json says 1.6.1, package-lock.json packages[\"\"] says 1.6.1.",
        "  make version of ncmake bumps info.xml, composer.json and package.json and re-syncs package-lock.json in one step, so they cannot drift apart. ncmake's lint-version workflow fails a push or a pull request on exactly this drift. The App Store and the server read info.xml, npm and composer read their own manifest. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying more than one version number, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ],
      "covers": [
        "lint-version/version-drift"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "link-dead",
      "lines": [
        "4 links of appinfo/info.xml lead nowhere:",
        "  <screenshot> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nextcloud/health/main/screenshots/health-start.png: HTTP 404",
        "  <screenshot small-thumbnail> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nextcloud/health/main/screenshots/health-preview.png: HTTP 404",
        "  <screenshot> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nextcloud/health/main/screenshots/health-person-start.png: HTTP 404",
        "  <screenshot> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nextcloud/health/main/screenshots/health-weight.png: HTTP 404",
        "  The App Store page shows these links as they are; a reader who follows one ends on an error page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 25 to 29; the oldest maintained major is 33 (the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  max-version 29 is below the oldest maintained major (33, the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), so the release covers only servers that no longer receive fixes.",
        "  min-version 25 reaches below the oldest maintained major (33), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "script-without-config",
      "lines": [
        "composer.json scripts psalm, psalm:update-baseline, psalm:fix, psalm:fix:dry call psalm, and no Psalm configuration is in the checkout.",
        "  ./vendor/bin/psalm --show-info=true --no-cache",
        "composer.json script test:unit runs phpunit with tests/unit/phpunit.xml, which is not in the checkout.",
        "  ./vendor/bin/phpunit -c tests/unit/phpunit.xml",
        "  The command is there to be run, so whoever runs it gets a tool that has nothing to go by - and CI, if it runs the script, reports the failure as the change under test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml, package.json), AGPL (composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  No SPDX id: agpl (package.json), AGPL (composer.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as >=20.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it.",
        "  The checks run on another Node: 16 (cypress.yml). They lint and test the code and build no release asset, so this decides only what those runs see."
      ]
    },
    {
